Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the assertion?$qb$, $qb$https://nsvaeqcsrlrvsmynwfft.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/question-images/CB-a2b0fc3b.png$qb$, $qb$[{"label": "A", "body": "around 50% urban in 1970 to around 90% urban in 2020."}, {"label": "B", "body": "less than 40% urban in 1970 to around 90% urban in 2020."}, {"label": "C", "body": "less than 20% urban in 1970 to more than 50% urban in 2020."}, {"label": "D", "body": "around 40% urban in 1970 to more than 70% urban in 2020."}]$qb$::jsonb, 'D'::answer_option, null, $qb$Choice D is the best answer. This choice effectively uses data from the graph to complete the example. The line representing the percent of
